| R1 | An agent justifies a second serial research prerequisite by consistency alone — "the sibling leaf has a gate, so this class needs one too", "the harness should also cover", symmetry with a prior leaf | **Refused.** A second serial prerequisite needs a checked spec gap (`solution-architect` rule 3: the missing piece, the requirement left incomplete, the spec sections checked) and its own budget; otherwise the finding is a focused regression in the owning leaf | Three nested gate leaves (contract gate, atom shapes, codepoints) were spawned from `repeat-of:` verdicts; production coverage stayed 0/28 vectors, 0/32 guards |
| R2 | Reuse of a green result after the harness, the source tree, the test tree, the configuration or the environment changed | **Refused.** Any changed identity makes the evidence about a different candidate; rerun with the diagnostic reason recorded. An earlier empty candidate never exempts a later source change | Reviewer anchors on a stale producer/revision are documented in two verdicts; a candidate was reviewed against a tree it no longer was |
| R3 | A gate claimed green with logs missing, truncated, unreadable, or ending before the last command | **Refused.** A failed or partial read is not a pass and not an absence; report which commands ran, which exit codes were observed, and mark the rest unrun. A cached `ok` on a package that reads files outside its module is this row | A 20-command suite timed out at command 13 of 20 after twelve greens; the seven unrun commands are unrun, not passed |
